From Carl Gable, Nov 8 2026: cases 1 and 2 of LaGriT's suite
test/suite/test_poisson_3d, with the box reduced to 0.4 x 0.4 x 0.2
(x, y, z in [0, 0.4] x [0, 0.4] x [0, 0.2]) to keep the files small.

  test_Poisson_3D_c1_c2.lgi        the LaGriT deck (runs cases 1, 2)
  test_run_createpts_poisson.mlgi  the macro it calls: createpts /
                                   poisson_disk / 3d_box ... connect,
                                   dump / avs, dump / stor
  test_3d_poi_01.inp, .stor        case 1: h = 0.025, no buffer on the
                                   outside surfaces (negative
                                   coefficients expected)
  test_3d_poi_02.inp, .stor        case 2: h = 0.025, buffer = h on the
                                   outside surfaces

The .stor files were written by LaGriT's dump / stor default,
anothermatbld3d ("matbld3d_astor" on line 2): compressed, with
coefficients equal within 1e-8 of the largest merged, and coefficients
below 1e-8 of the largest left out.

